{"name":"Alu Gobi","hex":"#ddbb00","fetched":"2026-10-21","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"alu","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for 'Are'are."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of aloo."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alu"},{"term":"gobi","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["cauliflower"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gobi"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aloo gobhi","blocks":[{"text":"Aloo gobhi, aloo gobi or alu gobhi is a vegetarian dish from the Indian subcontinent made with potatoes (aloo), cauliflower (gobhi), and Indian spices. It is popular in Indian cuisine. It is yellowish in color due to the use of turmeric, and occasionally contains black cumin and curry leaves. Other common ingredients include garlic, ginger, onion, coriander stalks, tomato, peas, black pepper, asafoetida and cumin. There are a number of variations and similar dishes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Aloo_Ghobi.jpg/330px-Aloo_Ghobi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aloo_gobhi","wikidata":"Q447296"},{"title":"Gobi Desert","blocks":[{"text":"The Gobi Desert is a large, cold desert and grassland region in southern Mongolia and North China. It is the sixth-largest desert in the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Gobi_Desert.jpg/330px-Gobi_Desert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gobi_Desert","wikidata":"Q42070"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Aloo_Ghobi.jpg/500px-Aloo_Ghobi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Aloo_Ghobi.jpg/1280px-Aloo_Ghobi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"htt